
  ▲ vercel whoami [options]

  Shows the username of the currently logged in user.                           

  Options:

  -F,  --format <FORMAT>  Specify the output format (json)                      
       --json             Output as JSON                                        


  Global Options:

       --cwd <DIR>            Sets the current working directory for a single   
                              run of a command                                  
  -d,  --debug                Debug mode (default off)                          
  -Q,  --global-config <DIR>  Path to the global `.vercel` directory            
  -h,  --help                 Output usage information                          
  -A,  --local-config <FILE>  Path to the local `vercel.json` file              
       --no-color             No color mode (default off)                       
       --non-interactive      Run without interactive prompts; when an agent is 
                              detected this is the default                      
  -S,  --scope                Set a custom scope                                
  -t,  --token <TOKEN>        Login token                                       
  -v,  --version              Output the version number                         


  Examples:

  - Shows the username of the currently logged in user

    $ vercel whoami

  Notes:

  On a terminal it also shows the active team and its plan. When piped, it      
  prints only the username.                                                     

  The active team comes from --scope, then the project linked in this directory,
  then the team saved by `vercel teams switch`, then your default team. It is   
  always a team: there is no personal account.                                  

  Exits with 1 when logged out.                                                 

  Related:

  vercel login         Sign in to your Vercel account.                        
  vercel teams switch  Switch to a different team                             


